<!--
  /overview — the SUI landing. Short, and it SHOWS. The argument lives on /why;
  this page must not restate it.

  Authored under `sui.config.json { preset: strict, sx: true }`: no <style>, no
  style=, no raw <div>/<span>. Layout is the keywords, surface is the primitives,
  everything else is sx. If a page cannot be built this way, that is a hole in the
  vocabulary — and this page is where we find out.
-->
<column class="doc landing" gap="5">
  <p class="eyebrow">SUI</p>
  <h1>The UI framework agents write</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Every decision a language leaves open is variance — and variance is where
    one-shot beauty dies. So the decisions are gone. What's left is 95% of the
    expression, with 10% of the choices. <a href="/why">The full argument →</a>
  </p>

  <h2>This is a component</h2>
  <p>
    No build config, no styling library, no component library to install. The
    tags below <em>are</em> the standard library, and they are already in your
    HTML vocabulary.
  </p>

  <center sx="py:8 px:4 bg:muted border:border radius:lg">
    <card motion:hover={{ scale: 'spring:gentle' }} sx="p:4 max-w:panel-max-w-md">
      <row gap="3" align="center">
        <avatar></avatar>
        <column gap="1">
          <strong>Ada Lovelace</strong>
          <p sx="fg:muted-foreground text:sm">Deploys on Fridays</p>
        </column>
        <badge tone="success">Active</badge>
      </row>
      <row gap="2" sx="mt:3">
        <button motion:press={{ scale: 'press' }}>Approve</button>
        <button variant="ghost">Dismiss</button>
      </row>
    </card>
  </center>
  <p sx="text:sm fg:muted-foreground">
    Hover the card. Press the button. That motion is one directive —
    <code>motion:hover</code> — not a library.
  </p>

  <h2>What's given</h2>
  <p>Not recommended. Not linted with a warning. <em>Absent</em>.</p>

  <grid cols="2" gap="3">
    <card interactive="true" sx="p:4">
      <a href="/elements"><strong>48 elements</strong></a>
      <p sx="text:sm fg:muted-foreground mt:1">
        A dialog is <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>. Half ship zero JavaScript; the
        rest compile away.
      </p>
    </card>
    <card interactive="true" sx="p:4">
      <a href="/styling"><strong>One way to style</strong></a>
      <p sx="text:sm fg:muted-foreground mt:1">
        An off-system color is a build error, not a review note.
      </p>
    </card>
    <card interactive="true" sx="p:4">
      <a href="/motion"><strong>One animation system</strong></a>
      <p sx="text:sm fg:muted-foreground mt:1">
        Eight triggers, nine presets. You cannot reach for a different library.
      </p>
    </card>
    <card interactive="true" sx="p:4">
      <a href="/behavior"><strong>One way to reach an element</strong></a>
      <p sx="text:sm fg:muted-foreground mt:1">
        <code>use:</code>. No ref to thread, no escape hatch to be tempted by.
      </p>
    </card>
  </grid>

  <row class="page-nav" gap="2">
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/getting-started">Getting started →</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/why">Why SUI</a>
    <a class="btn" href="/tutorial">Try the tutorial</a>
  </row>
</column>
